<title>USA: Loyola University, Ill., $188 mln bonds repriced.</title>
<headline>Loyola University, Ill., $188 mln bonds repriced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc. said Tuesday it repriced and restructured Illinois Health Facilities Authority's $188 million bond deal for Loyola University, adjusting yields in several maturities and raising the top yield in 2024 to 5.63 percent from 5.60 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>ILLINOIS HEALTH FACILITIES AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $187,555,000*</p>
<p>REVENUE BONDS, SERIES 1997A</p>
<p>(LOYOLA UNIVERSITY HEALTH SYSTEM)</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD. NOTE REPRICING AND RESTRUCTURING.</p>
